direction: down
title: Java Memory Model (JMM) Hardware Cache Coherence Architecture

RAM: Main System Memory (RAM) {
  style.fill: "#0B132B"
  style.stroke: "#0284C7"
  flag: "Shared Variable: boolean flag = false"
}

Core1: CPU Core 1 (Thread 1: Writer) {
  style.fill: "#1C1917"
  style.stroke: "#8B5CF6"
  l1: "L1 Cache & Store Buffer: flag = true (Unflushed!)"
  code: "flag = true (without volatile, write is buffered locally)"
}

Core2: CPU Core 2 (Thread 2: Reader) {
  style.fill: "#1C1917"
  style.stroke: "#EF4444"
  l1: "L1 Cache: flag == false (Stale hit!)"
  loop: "while(!flag) spins forever (Liveness failure)"
}

VolatileFix: The Volatile Remedy {
  style.fill: "#06201B"
  style.stroke: "#10B981"
  barriers: "StoreLoad Memory Barrier: Flushes store buffer to RAM; invalidates reader L1 cache"
}

Core1 -> RAM: Non-volatile write stays in local buffer
RAM -> Core2: Reader misses update; uses stale L1 cache
